ctive_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n* Reproducible in: Godot version 4.6 dev 6 (standard build)\n* ***Not*** reproducible in: Godot version 4.6 dev 5 (standard build)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev6 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9144) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-14900KF (32 threads) - 63.83 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nOpening a barebones SubViewport scene with a WorldEnvironment child causes errors to constantly repeat while in 3D view.\n\nThe following errors repeat seemingly every frame:\n```\nERROR: Create(Graphics)PipelineState failed with error 0x80070057.\nERROR: servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp:4224 - Condition \"!pipeline.driver_id\" is true. Returning: RID()\nERROR: servers/rendering/renderer_rd/pipeline_cache_rd.cpp:59 - Condition \"pipeline.is_null()\" is true. Returning: RID()\nERROR: servers/rendering/rendering_device.cpp:4665 - Parameter \"pipeline\" is null.\nERROR: This render pipeline requires (0) bytes of push constant data, supplied: (64)\nERROR: No render pipeline was set before attempting to draw.\n```\n\nThese errors appear even if the SubViewport has \"Disable 3D\" checked.\n\nThese errors do not appear in the 2D view.\n\nThese errors do not appear to show up with that subviewport as an instance in a scene with a SubViewportContainer while in game (though I could have configured it incorrectly since I've never used them before).\n\nChanging \"Rendering > Rendering Device > Driver.windows\" to \"vulkan\" and restarting the editor fixes the issue.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n\nProject is just a brand new project using the \"Mobile\" renderer, with the following steps taken:\n* A basic SubViwport as the main scene, with a WorldEnvironment 